# The break's frame is for a break that is heard. Rest in the middle of one and the rest's screen or the page is up, by PLAY or by MIDI Stop; it comes back with the sound. In Auto, a break the arranger plays with the drums muted or at level 0 leaves the page alone
wait 3000
press SEL
tap SEQ
release SEL
wait 3000
expect level >1
# ---- PLAY, in a called break, on Home
press SEL
tap EDIT
release SEL
wait 1700
expect breakbars >0
expect screen 3
expect view 0
tap PLAY
wait 200
expect playing 0
expect screen 6
wait 5000
expect playing 0
expect screen 6
# a page's button, resting: the page
tap ENV
wait 400
expect view 1
expect screen 2
tap HOME
wait 400
expect screen 6
# ---- and back: the break goes on where it stopped, its frame with it, and ends
tap PLAY
wait 60
expect playing 1
expect breakbars >0
expect screen 3
wait 7000
expect breakbars 0
expect screen 1
# ---- MIDI Stop in a called break, MIDI Continue
press SEL
tap EDIT
release SEL
wait 1700
expect breakbars >0
expect screen 3
midi FC 00 00
wait 200
expect playing 0
expect screen 6
midi FB 00 00
wait 60
expect playing 1
expect screen 3
wait 7000
expect breakbars 0
expect screen 1

# ---- Auto, the arranger's breaks: the frame, with the drums on (counted, frame by frame: when each break comes is the arranger's)
reboot
press SEL
tap HOME
release SEL
wait 100
style jungle
energy 100
breaks 100
seed 11
wait 40000
expect mode 0
expect brkshown >0
expect brkquiet 0
expect brkwrong 0
# ---- the same at level 0: breaks composed as ever, and no frame
setpar 16 0
expect par16 0
drawreset
wait 40000
expect brkquiet >60
expect brkwrong 0
# ---- the same, muted: a page stays a page
setpar 16 45
wait 8000
expect level >1
press SEL
tap SEQ
release SEL
wait 100
expect mutedrums 1
tap ENV
drawreset
wait 80000
expect mutedrums 1
expect view 1
expect brkquiet >60
expect brkwrong 0
